# programs/jalwa_play_probe.cyr — the jalwa->mishran agnos audio proof (single-process).
#
# Proves jalwa's decoded audio flows THROUGH the mishran mixer to the sovereign
# audio output on agnos: decode /tone.wav (shravan) -> feed the PCM over the mishran
# WIRE (msh_send WRITE/loopback:7701) to an IN-PROCESS mishran server -> msh_router_pump
# mixes it -> vani audio_* -> sys_snd_* #64-69 -> HDA DAC. Single-process (client +
# server + sink in one binary, sh_exec'd) sidesteps the two-proc scheduling of a
# separate mishrand daemon (a separate agnos-kernel concern); the full data path —
# jalwa decode, the msh wire protocol + backpressure ring, the mixer, the vani sink —
# is exercised end-to-end. Includes the SAME module assembly as src/main.cyr (minus
# the CLI entry) so jlw_audio_decode + its deps resolve. Prints markers the smoke gates on.
#
# Build:  cyrius build --agnos programs/jalwa_play_probe.cyr build/jalwa-play-probe

# ===== ASSEMBLY: all modules (mirrors src/main.cyr) =====
